HOW SQL EXECUTES GROUPBY
1. FROM       ──> Identifies target table(s)
2. WHERE      ──> Filters out raw rows
3. GROUP BY   ──> Organizes remaining rows into groups
4. HAVING     ──> Filters out entire groups
5. SELECT     ──> Computes aggregates & returns selected columns
6. ORDER BY   ──> Sorts final output
7. LIMIT      ──> Restricts output row count
